# THE COPY MADE BEFORE THE END IS THE RUNTIME'S (panel 177's items 1, 3 and
# 4, 2026-09-25). `keep = a` is a second name for the same address, and the
# checker's rule tracks the NAME the ending call was handed: `keep` was handed
# to nothing, so nothing at check time is dead, `check` 0. This is the class
# design.md Part 8 wart 20 states, the compiler-engineer's E13, and it is why
# the compile-time half is a half: the runtime stops the copy before C.
# It stopped it as a handle given back that the set no longer held until the
# runtime's half landed beside this one; since then the dead set remembers the
# address the first release ended, and names the copy at its first crossing.
extern "handle-a-copy-made-before-the-end-is-the-runtime-s.h"
    record Node tag node
    function node_new(v: i64) -> Node acquires node_free
    function node_free(n: Node consumes)
    function node_peek(n: Node) -> i64

function main()
    a = node_new(v: 5)
    keep = a
    print("through the copy: ", node_peek(n: keep))
    node_free(n: a)
    node_free(n: keep)
    print("not reached")
